[Enter Prospero and Miranda]
Prospero:
 You are as good as the product of Viola and Viola.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and the product of the sum of a big big hero and a hero and the product of Ophelia and Romeo.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and a hero.
 You are as good as the difference between yourself and a hero.
 You are as good as the remainder of the quotient between yourself and Hamlet.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and a hero.
 Open your heart.
[Exeunt]

